# Normalise line endings in the repository AND in the working copy.
#
# Why: Git on Windows defaults to core.autocrlf=true, which rewrites LF to CRLF
# on checkout. Three consequences this project cares about:
#
#   1. A file's bytes on disk stop matching its bytes in the repository, so
#      hash comparison between what was written and what is there stops being
#      a valid check. Invariant 2 says verify by content; that is only
#      meaningful if the content is stable.
#   2. The packaged zip's contents would depend on a local git setting rather
#      than on the commit, so two people building the same commit could produce
#      two different artifacts.
#   3. Diffs become noise the first time a file is touched on another machine.
#
# LF everywhere. Chrome does not care, PowerShell 5.1 does not care, and it
# keeps "compare the bytes" a real instruction.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary, never line-ending converted, never diffed as text
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.ico  binary
*.webp binary
*.zip  binary
*.crx  binary
*.pem  binary
